From 8bb923afa861557851f5d80a5cf02b46bac7013a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:33:48 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Muse Spark family: muse_spark on the shared EXL3
 operators, fp16 KV, TP=2 over fabric/tp, DFlash2, prompt cache

The family serves an EXL3 pack of Muse Spark Open's text model on the native CUDA server, one GPU or two DGX Sparks
as tensor-parallel ranks (rank 1: tf-muse follow).

- EXL3 projections and routed experts run on main's shared operators: cuda.exl3 Linear (tf_exl3_rot_in,
  tf_exl3_linear_*) and cuda.exl3_experts (group, rotate, tf_exl3_grouped_2, the fp32 SwiGLU epilogue, down).
- Family kernels: attention.cu (head dim 64, GQA 8:1 decode attention, fp16 cache), glue.cu (norms, gated
  residuals, fp32 router, top-8, expert norms and sums, softcap, argmax, RoPE tables), linear_multi.cu (q/k/v/gate
  in one launch and 32-row passes over exl3_decode.cuh, the shared linear's bits), experts2.cu (32-member tiles of
  the shared grouped GEMM for prompt windows, its bits), dflash.cu and dflash2.cu (the drafter).
- A row's bits do not depend on its window, the graph bucket or prompt chunking; the prompt cache keeps states
  through the snap_* hooks; the family declares its memory reserve and prompt-cache budget defaults.
- tf-muse m1 / prompt / dflash / drafted checks and test-muse host tests; docs/recipes/muse-spark.md.
